Privacy Policy
Flycar Arc Runway
Contact: [nguyentantruong8126@icloud.com]

This Privacy Policy explains how Flycar Arc Runway (“the App,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) handles information when you use the App on Apple devices.

1. Summary
Flycar Arc Runway is designed as an offline, single-player entertainment app.
We do not require an account, do not operate an online service for gameplay, and do not sell personal data. Game progress and settings are stored only on your device.

2. Information We Collect
We do not collect personal information from you through the App.

In particular, the App does not collect or request:

Name, email address, phone number, or account credentials
Precise or approximate location
Contacts, photos, microphone, camera (beyond optional on-device photo features you choose to use and that remain on your device, if available)
Advertising identifiers (such as IDFA) for advertising or cross-app tracking
Payment or financial information through the App’s core gameplay
Health, fitness, or other sensitive personal data
Local data stored on your device may include:

Game progress (levels completed, scores, stars, achievements)
Vehicle unlocks / upgrades and related gameplay preferences
App settings (for example language, volume, haptics, assist options)
Other gameplay-related files saved in the App’s local storage
This local data stays on your device unless you choose to back up your device through Apple services (for example iCloud Backup), which are controlled by Apple under Apple’s own policies.

3. How We Use Information
Because we do not collect personal information through the App, we do not use personal information for advertising, analytics profiles, marketing lists, or resale.

Local on-device data is used only to:

Save and restore your gameplay progress and settings
Provide the features you select inside the App
4. Sharing of Information
We do not share, sell, rent, or disclose personal information to third parties through the App, because we do not collect it.

The App is not designed to transmit your gameplay data to our servers.

5. Third-Party Services
The App’s core experience is intended to work without requiring third-party analytics, advertising, social login, or online multiplayer services.

If you use Apple platform features (for example App Store, device backups, or system photo saving), those features are provided by Apple and governed by Apple’s Privacy Policy:
https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/

6. Tracking
We do not use App Tracking Transparency for cross-app tracking, and we do not track you across other companies’ apps or websites for advertising.

7. Children’s Privacy
The App does not knowingly collect personal information from children. Because the App does not collect personal information, it does not create online accounts or profiles for users of any age.

If you believe a child has provided personal information to us through another channel (for example by emailing us), contact us and we will delete that information from our correspondence records where applicable.

8. Data Retention and Deletion
Gameplay data is retained on your device until you:

Delete the App, or
Clear/reset App data using your device controls (where available), or
Use any in-app reset option if provided
Uninstalling the App removes the App’s local data from that device, subject to any separate device backups you maintain.

9. Data Security
We rely on the security of your device and Apple’s operating system sandboxing to protect locally stored App data. No method of electronic storage is 100% secure. Please keep your device locked and updated.

10. International Users
The App stores gameplay data locally on your device. We do not operate a gameplay cloud database that transfers your personal information internationally through the App.

11. Your Choices
You can:

Play without creating an account
Change language and other settings inside the App
Stop all App use by uninstalling the App
Manage device backups in your Apple device settings
12. Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Effective date” at the top will be revised when changes are posted. Continued use of the App after an update means you acknowledge the revised Policy.

